 <office:body>
  <office:text>
   <text:sequence-decls>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Illustration"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Table"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Text"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Drawing"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Figure"/>
   </text:sequence-decls>
   <table:table table:name="Table2" table:style-name="Table2">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table2.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table2.B"/>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table2.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P6"><text:span text:style-name="T12"><text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T17">Green Paper</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table2.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P7">G P <text:span text:style-name="T12">Moringa </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20">CA</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table2.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:h text:style-name="P8" text:outline-level="1"><text:span text:style-name="T2">Moringa</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T4">and</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T20">Wild Rice</text:span></text:h>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table2.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P21"><text:span text:style-name="T18"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P21"><text:span text:style-name="T18"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P21"><text:span text:style-name="T18"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P21"><text:span text:style-name="T18">Revised April </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T19">13</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T18">, 2026</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:h text:style-name="P20" text:outline-level="2"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Overview</text:span></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P22">Combining moringa and wild rice creates a nutrient-dense, high-fiber meal that pairs the &quot;superfood&quot; benefits of the Miracle Tree with the earthy, nutty profile of aquatic grass seeds. While traditional recipes often use white or brown rice, wild rice adds significantly more fiber and protein to the dish. </text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Health Benefits</text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Nutrient Powerhouse</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23">Moringa is rich in Vitamins A, C, and B-complex, as well as iron, calcium, and magnesium.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Heart &amp; Blood Health</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P24">Moringa <text:span text:style-name="T23">has may health benefits, including </text:span>lower blood pressure and cholesterol. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P24"><text:span text:style-name="T23">W</text:span>ild rice provides fiber needed for cardiovascular support.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Dietary Fiber</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23">Wild rice has a higher fiber content than white <text:span text:style-name="T23">or brown</text:span> rice, which aids digestion and supports weight management. </text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P20" text:outline-level="2"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Recipes</text:span></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23">You can incorporate these two ingredients in several ways:<text:note text:id="ftn0" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>1</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
      <text:p text:style-name="Footnote">https://saucyseattleite.com/2015/03/wild-rice-crispy-treats/</text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Moringa Wild Rice Stir-Fry</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23">Sauté aromatics like onions, garlic, and ginger, then add cooked wild rice and fresh moringa leaves or moringa powder.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Harvest Bowls</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23">Mix wild rice with moringa <text:span text:style-name="T23">(leaves or powder)</text:span>, roasted vegetables, and nuts like cashews or peanuts for a protein-rich lunch.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Hearty Soups</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23">Add wild rice and moringa powder to a turkey or beef vegetable soup for a boost in vitamins and minerals.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Rice Khichdi</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23">Combine wild rice with lentils and moringa powder for a one-pot comfort meal. </text:p>
  </office:text>
 </office:body>
</office:document>